Acceptance criteria

The implementation is complete when all of the following are true:

A fighter takes a normal hit and receives the existing Launch Point increase. That current hit uses the new increased Launch Point for its launch calculation exactly as before.

If that fighter then receives no genuine hit for 2 full seconds, nothing has yet been removed.

After another 0.5 seconds, exactly 1 Launch Point is removed.

Every following 0.5 seconds without another genuine hit removes exactly 1 more.

Recovery stops at 0 and can never produce a negative Launch Point.

Any later genuine unblocked hit immediately:

* adds its normal damage;
* uses the resulting new Launch Point for that hit’s launch;
* discards all previous recovery timing/progress;
* starts a fresh 2-second grace period.

A Shielded/blocked attack:

* adds no Launch Point as before;
* causes no launch as before;
* does not restart Launch recovery.

The behavior works identically for every fighter and every normal hit source, including non-launching hits.

Respawn/restart produces clean Launch Point 0 and clean recovery state.

Discover, the product specification, system documentation, README/comments where applicable, and the gameplay implementation all describe the same rule.

All existing and new tests pass.

